---
title: Vigenère cipher
tags: tools
summary: >-
    Shifts each letter of the message by the matching letter of a key, which starts again from its first letter when it runs out.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>One of the best-known ciphers. <code class="tool-example">Hello</code> encrypted with the key <code class="tool-example">World</code> shifts like <code class="tool-example">H → W → D</code> <code class="tool-example">e → o → s</code> <code class="tool-example">l → r → c</code> <code class="tool-example">l → l → w</code> <code class="tool-example">o → d → r</code>, and a sixth letter would use the W in World again.</p>
    <p>More on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vigen%C3%A8re_cipher" class="text-convrtr">Vigenère cipher</a> Wikipedia page.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Vigenère cipher", placeholder = "Example: Hello → World [key] → Dscwr") %}
<div class="input-group w-auto">
    <label class="input-group-text" for="{{ filename }}Key"><span class="visually-hidden">Vigenère </span>Key</label>
    <input type="text" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}Key" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Status">
    <button class="btn btn-convrtr" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Encrypt" aria-pressed="true">Encrypt</button>
    <button class="btn btn-outline-convrtr" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Decrypt" aria-pressed="false">Decrypt</button>
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
